<!DOCTYPE suzuki [
<!ENTITY % sdatacharaents SYSTEM "..\config8\sdatacharaents.txt">
%sdatacharaents;
]>
<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "10A">
<servcat sctnbr = "10" scnbr = "01">
<configtype typenbr = "2">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0AA126002" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Millimeter Wave Radar Aiming Adjustment
</title>
<ptxt>
Perform “Millimeter Wave Radar Aiming Adjustment” as follows.
</ptxt>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove RBS control module inner cover.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Perform 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA126002001">Vehicle Preparation</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Perform 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA126002002">Inspection of Reflector Plate</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Perform 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA126002003">Set Up of Special Tool</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Perform 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA126002004">Aiming Adjustment</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Perform 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA126002005">Inspection of RBS Control Module Bracket</intxref>
 if necessary.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install RBS control module inner cover.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AA126002001">
<title>
Vehicle Preparation
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Park vehicle on level surface where no obstacles or reflectors in front of the vehicle in the area of 2.5 m (8.2 ft.) ahead, 5.0 m (16.4 ft.) wide (2.5 m (8.2 ft.) on both sides from center of millimeter wave radar device), and 2.0 m (6.6 ft.) high.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Metal reflects millimeter wave. Check that there is no metallic material on the floor surface.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0AAA1020.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "45.048mm" ver = "01" gw = "227" gh = "111"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
“a”:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
2.5 m (8.2 ft.)
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
“c”:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
2.0 m (6.6 ft.)
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
“b”:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
5.0 m (16.4 ft.)
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Adjust air pressure of all tires to specified value.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove any load from vehicle.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
It is not necessary to empty the fuel tank.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Clean millimeter wave radar surface (1) and check that there is no adhesion of water droplets etc. or abrasion.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IDK80QAA0025.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "54.514mm" ver = "02" gw = "164" gh = "138"/>
</figure>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AA126002002">
<title>
Inspection of Reflector Plate
</title>
<ptxt>
Check the following items about reflector plate (special tool: 09932 – 36540).
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
No adhesion of dirt on reflector plate surface
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
No abrasion on reflector plate surface
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
No distortion of reflector plate
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AA126002003" page = "1">
<title>
Set Up of Special Tool
</title>
<attention4>
<ptxt>
Failure to take the following precautions could cause inaccurate reflection of millimeter wave.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
During storage or set up of reflector plate, do not damage its reflecting surface protecting it by packing material or cloth.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Do not distort reflector plate exposing it to large shock or stress.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention4>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Reflecting surface of new reflector plate is covered by protective film and millimeter wave could not be reflected without removing the film. Remove the protective film from the reflector plate before setting up.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Put rear reflector frame (1) in contact with rear wheels (2) and set the frame so that dimension “a” from the frame right end to right tire center becomes as shown.
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Rear reflector frame setting position
</title>
<ptxt>
“a”: 1,055 – 1,105 mm (41.54 – 43.50 in.)
</ptxt>
</spec>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect front reflector frame (3) and rear reflector frame using reflector wire ropes (4).
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Set up of special tools cannot be done correctly if reflector wire ropes are crimped.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
Undo entangled ropes carefully, if any. Do not pull ropes entangled.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Stretch right and left reflector wire ropes equally so that center line of RBS control module (5) aligns with center of front reflector frame.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L10A203">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09932-36531">
09932–36531
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
<servicetoolitem id = "L10A204">
<s-part>
(B)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09932-36550">
09932–36550
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0AA12015.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "90.380mm" ver = "01" gw = "453" gh = "240"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Clean reflector plate (1) and check that there is no adhesion of dirt or abrasion.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set reflector plate to position 2 as shown.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check that set up distance “a” from front end (millimeter wave radar surface) of RBS control module (2) to reflector plate is as specified. If the distance is not within the specification, repeat Step 1) – 3) again.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L10A205">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09932-36540">
09932–36540
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<spec>
<title>
Reflector plate set up distance
</title>
<ptxt>
“a”: 1.0 – 1.1 m (3.3 – 3.6 ft.)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0AA12016.jpg" width = "183.000mm" height = "61.395mm" ver = "01" gw = "475" gh = "158"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "6" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.968in"/>
<colspec colnum = "5" colname = "5" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "6" colname = "6" colwidth = "1.968in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[a]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 1
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[b]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 2
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "5" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[c]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "6" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 3
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Adjust front reflector frame (5) to be vertical checking inclination of the frame putting level (2) to center of reflector plate (1) at the top and bottom in turn, and turning adjuster pads (4).
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
While putting level to the top and bottom of reflector plate, check an air bubble (3) in the level becomes just center as a result of the adjustment.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L10A206">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09932-36531">
09932–36531
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
<servicetoolitem id = "L10A207">
<s-part>
(B)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09932-36540">
09932–36540
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEAA0BAA0032.swf" width = "183.000mm" height = "86.550mm" ver = "02" gw = "465" gh = "229"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set reflector plate to position 1.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0AA126002004" page = "2">
<title>
Aiming Adjustment
</title>
<attention4>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
If DTC C1600 is detected, aiming adjustment cannot be done. In this case, it is necessary to perform troubleshooting first.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
When “Result of wave intensity measurement” at position 1 – 3 is “Incomplete”, DTC C1610 will be detected.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention4>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect SUZUKI scan tool to DLC (1) with ignition “OFF”.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L10A208">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "NNNNN-00035">
SUZUKI scan tool (Suzuki SDT-II)
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGSB0AAA1023.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "87.737mm" ver = "01" gw = "205" gh = "232"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition “ON”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Select “Aiming” under “Utility” mode in “Adaptive Cruise Control”.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set reflector plate (1) to position 1 and check that the plate is completely stationary. And then, select “Next” in SUZUKI scan tool.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Upon selection of “Next”, measurement of regulated radio wave intensity at position 1 is started.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEAA0BAA0033.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "91.237mm" ver = "02" gw = "227" gh = "242"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[a]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 1
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[c]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 3
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[b]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 2
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
When “Result of wave intensity measurement” at position 1 becomes “Complete”, set reflector plate (1) to position 2 and check that the plate is completely stationary. And then, select “Next” in SUZUKI scan tool.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
If “Incomplete” stays displayed for 5 seconds after starting measurement of regulated radio wave intensity, inadequate set up of reflector plate is assumed. Check the state of 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AA126002003">Set Up of Special Tool</intxref>
. If set up of the special tools is correct, malfunction of RBS control module is suspected.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEAA0BAA0034.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "101.955mm" ver = "02" gw = "227" gh = "272"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[a]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 1
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[c]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 3
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[b]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 2
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
When “Result of wave intensity measurement” at position 2 becomes “Complete”, set reflector plate (1) to position 3 and check that the plate is completely stationary. And then, select “Next” in SUZUKI scan tool.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEAA0BAA0035.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "101.895mm" ver = "02" gw = "227" gh = "272"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "1">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[a]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 1
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[c]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 3
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
[b]:
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Position 2
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
When “Result of wave intensity measurement” at position 3 is finished with “Complete” displayed, adjust direction of millimeter wave radar surface turning aiming bolts (1). Follow turning value of adjustment for up and down and right and left shown on the display.
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
For adjustment of aiming bolts, use commercially available 3.5 mm socket driver (2).
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
If there is no allowance for the bolt adjustment or turning values for adjustment for “up/down” and/or “right/left” is shown as “&#177; 8.00”, suspend aiming adjustment by selecting “Cancel” and perform the following steps.
</ptxt>
</item>
<list2 type = "ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Check reflector plate. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0AA126002002"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Recheck the state of special tool set up. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0AA126002003"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check RBS control module for loose or faulty fitting.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check RBS control module bracket. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0AA126002005"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check vehicle body for distortion.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check front bumper member for distortion.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check RBS control module itself.
</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IEAA0BAA0036.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "62.200mm" ver = "02" gw = "224" gh = "160"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list2>
</list1>
</attention3>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "ILSB0AA12017.jpg" width = "88.000mm" height = "135.228mm" ver = "01" gw = "232" gh = "367"/>
<callout>
